<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The W26 floor lane ~ one owner per registry, the floor by CID

Roadmap row `W26` carries the build of two operator rulings: //the system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor// (2026-10-16) and //one owner per registry; the floor reads by CID// (2026-10-18), both at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> #/rulings. Rows `W21` and `P8` ride it. The law it enacts already stands at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">> #/oracle-planes: an oracle names documents at one scope, that scope's owner writes its registry, and a registry travels no wider than its scope.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-shape>>

!! The shape

```text
  CONTENT PLANE (CAS)   immutable bytes by CID: engine, grammar, plugins, corpus snapshots.
                        Anyone reads; nobody writes in place; a herm carries and never reads private bytes.

  FLOOR                 a manifest CID naming the lares and lararium snapshots and the engine.
                        Read-only and history-free. Genesis carries the first floor.
  RELEASE ANSWER        one per Nexus, on its crossroads board: the Nexus AID, the charter epoch,
                        the release before it, the floor manifest CID. The steward seals it; the
                        cabal approves its exact bytes; a herm carries it and signs nothing.
  @oracle               the floor's read-face, mounted under every wiki by the pin its face
                        accepted. Never a document any vessel writes.

  REGISTRIES, each written by its own scope's owner alone
    vessel bootstrap    this vessel: its daemon url, its own document pointers, its face planes,
                        its accepted floor pin per (face, Nexus) as sealed hot rows
    @catalog            the operator's documents, at the operator's scope
    Kahu realm          the cabal: the LIVE lares and lararium documents and their drafts
    crossroads board    the Nexus: its one public answer, the release

  A WIKI                a recipe over bags: @oracle floor (pinned CID, read-only) < libraries
                        (read-only) < its own canon (promotion only) < @working (every save
                        lands here) < @draft, @personal, @temp. An edit copies up; a promotion
                        moves down by receipt; system canon moves only as a Kahu-cabal promotion
                        in the realm, and reaches everyone else only as a release.
```

''What the shape answers.'' The `lares` and `lararium` documents live in one place, the Kahu realm of the Nexus whose cabal writes them; on a lone hearth that realm belongs to its operator, who stands as its own Kahu. Every other vessel holds their snapshots by CID. A vessel's own pointers rest in its own bootstrap, so no shared document hosts another vessel's url and nothing merges across siblings. A wiki's floor moves only on a person's accept of a signed release, face by face, so one vessel may hold two Nexuses' floors and ties no face to another.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-evidence>>

!! The evidence that drew it (2026-10-18, lane `--w26-own-canon`)

* ''The shared document merges siblings' pointers.'' `oracleGenesisDocUrl()` gives every vessel one id, and each vessel writes its own `lares` and `lararium` urls, crossroads pin and realm pointers into it (`genesis-artifact.ts` `mintLaresIfAbsent`, `who-face.ts`, `realm-plane.ts`). Two vessels that each mint their own `lares` document settle on ONE `LARES_DOC_URI` once they sync; the control, never connected, keeps each its own (`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/shared-oracle-doc.probe.test.ts`).
* ''The split moves rather than closes.'' With the lares wiki's own canon held to its granted document, `herm-reshares-public-blob` step ③ failed three of three runs: the MOVE landed in A's document while `wiki which` and sync read the document the shared plane named. A's log in each run: `layer lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lararium moved …` then `layer lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lares held at …; the shared plane names …`. A's lares wiki then mounted the joinee's lararium corpus, the reverse of `W21`'s ruling.
* ''One signed floor object stands, and it names no Nexus.'' `OraclePointer` (domain `oracle-pointer`) signs a cid, heads and parents under the vessel seed (`oracle-substrate.ts`, `mountOracleReadFace`); readers pin the hearth's key.
* ''The system bags mount writable everywhere.'' `slotLayerFlags` marks every slot but `@oracle` writable, and every vessel registers `lares` and `lararium` as its own ground (`register-bags.ts` `OWN_GROUND`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-slices>>

!! The slices ~ each red-first, in the order what inherits shape from what

# ''The floor.'' A manifest CID names history-free snapshots of the `lares` and `lararium` rows beside the engine CIDs; `@oracle` mounts as its read-face, read-only, under every recipe; genesis bakes the first floor, its corpus CID in the seed, in one labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE`. Red: a minted wiki reads a system carrier through `@oracle` and its write refuses.
# ''Pointers go home.'' Each vessel's own document pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap; the shared `@oracle` document as a writable registry retires. `shared-oracle-doc.probe` turns into this slice's red: two synced vessels each keep their own pointer. `W21` re-cuts here: a joinee mounts its hearth's floor by CID.
# ''The live system documents rest in the Kahu realm.'' A one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group; `kahuCabalCanonAccess` gains its production caller; `bags/` projects on the Kahu's vessel alone. Red: a lone hearth's `working-loop` promotion lands, and a second vessel holds no live system document.
# ''The release answer.'' One porch body per Nexus, sealed by the steward under its own signing domain (house lean `floor-release`, awaiting the operator's word), the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes attached; the crossroads board carries it; `P8` folds in. `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN` retires once releases stand.
# ''The accept act.'' A person's act moves a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) to a newer release that verifies against that Nexus's charter at its epoch and links to the pinned release; no clock and no automatic accept. With no Nexus speaking, a face stands on its last accepted floor, or genesis.
# ''Reach into system canon.'' Every residency verb into `bags/lares` or `bags/lararium` refuses a hand outside the Kahu cabal, through the one predicate slice 3 seats; the skipped red in `unbuilt-laws.test.ts` ("a non-Kahu MOVE into a canon bag refuses") greens here.

''Beside the slices.'' `herm-reshares-public-blob` re-aims onto a public user bag: it tests a herm's re-share of a public blob, and a peer's write into system canon belongs to the Kahu alone. The re-aim travels to the mesh-goldens lane as a patch, beside the layer instrument that measured step ③.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-retires>>

!! What retires, slice by slice (the o-takiage census)

* `lares` and `lararium` in every vessel's `OWN_GROUND` (`register-bags.ts`), and `mintLaresIfAbsent` / `mintLarariumIfAbsent` on a vessel outside the cabal (`genesis-artifact.ts`): slices 2 and 3.
* The shared document's per-vessel rows: the system pointers, `registerCrossroadsInOracle`, `realm-plane.ts`'s realm pointer and steward nym: slice 2.
* recipe-watch's oracle loop over the system slots (`recipe-watch.ts`): slice 2, which leaves it nothing to follow.
* `W21`'s lares-pointer patch at reconcile and the oracle crossing of `device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`: slice 2.
* `OraclePointer` and `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN`: slice 4.
* Canon lines that name "the shared floor CID" (`oracle-governance#/board-model`, `pronaos#/the-rung-ladder`) and the docblocks that call the oracle "the vessel's own plane" or libraries "read-only from wiki": the slice whose code makes each line true.

''The interim cure stays out.'' The lane's recipe-watch hold (`--w26-own-canon`, commit `d1983aa75`) keeps a system wiki's own canon against a shared pointer that slice 2 removes; under //build the end state// it lands nowhere. Its probes stand: the shared-oracle probe as slice 2's red, the `W25` creator probe as that row's measurement.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-lane>>

!! The lane ~ crew and crucible

* ''Branch'': `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--w26-floor-<n>`, one per slice or burst, cut from the span's head. Nothing lands on the span directly.
* ''Crew'': the work swarm (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-shapes): an Opus Episkopos, a Sol-6 and a Luna-6 in one provisioned worktree, walled per #/the-launch; spirits build and write red tests, and the lead runs every suite. Every slice moves facts between processes (a vessel and its islands, a vessel and its siblings), so the overwatch reads every burst.
* ''Shared ground'': both vessel composers. One lane at a time holds a composer hunk; the others hand theirs to the controller as a patch. Slice 1's re-bake and every plugin-bundle rebuild land on the controller's word.
* ''The crucible'': each touched package's whole suite under a scratch `HOME` and `LAR_ROOT`, `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`, one shard run with its `MERGE-VERIFY` line, a pull request into the span with no Copilot review unless the operator asks; the controller runs `tools/witness-all.sh` and merges.

<<~/ahu>>

